---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro'
import { translations } from '../../../i18n/landing'
// Eine Seite fuer jede Sprache (Starlight lokalisiert Sidebar-Links), der Inhalt bleibt Englisch.
export function getStaticPaths() {
  return [{ params: { lang: undefined } }, ...Object.keys(translations).filter((l) => l !== 'de').map((lang) => ({ params: { lang } }))]
}
import { packages, REPO } from '../../../lib/reference'
---
<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title: 'Packages', description: 'The packages of Real Life Stack on npm and what each is for.', tableOfContents: false }}>
  <p>An app installs three of these: the contract, the toolkit and one connector. The versions live on npm; the release process is described under <a href="/handbuch/release/">Versionen und Releases</a> (German).</p>
  <div class="rl-table rl-ref rl-packages">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Package</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {packages.map((p) => (
          <tr>
            <td><code>{p.name}</code><div class="rl-links"><a href={`https://www.npmjs.com/package/${p.name}`}>npm</a><a href={`${REPO}packages/${p.dir}`}>source</a></div></td>
            <td>{p.description}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Subpaths of the toolkit: <code>@real-life-stack/toolkit/router</code> (frame with URL focus, needs <code>react-router-dom</code>), <code>/maplibre</code> and <code>/leaflet</code> (map engines), <code>/styles/globals.css</code> (tokens).</p>
</StarlightPage>
